# "good will" in S2, S4, S5 and S6 means the same thing: the will that governs how gifts are used and that makes up character.
# "pleasure" in S5 and in A1 is the same claim, an impartial spectator approving of the sight. A1 is its converse, applied to the worthy being, not a shift in sense.
